Regression tests, run on the QEMU target.

Build the tree with make first, then run

	usr/local/test/run		all tests
	usr/local/test/run sh awk	only the named tests

Each test boots boot/unix on a fresh copy of the root file system, with
the programs compiled from t/*.c and the data files from t/ installed in
/t. The script prints one PASS or FAIL line per test and exits non-zero
if any test failed, keeping the outputs in the directory it names.

A test is cases/NAME.steps, the session to type; cases/NAME.exp, the
expected output; and optionally cases/NAME.sed, which normalises output
that legitimately varies, such as dates, clock ticks, and addresses.

A plain line of a steps file is typed at the shell prompt, or at the
here-document prompt. A line @expect|send waits for expect, then types
send, in which \n is a newline, ^C is DEL, and ^D is EOT; expect may
contain \xNN. Type the erase and kill characters # and @ as \# and \@.
